 ## Background
-Chunk-based rendering originated as a solution to rendering lag in voxel engines, particularly in the context of games like Minecraft [S1, S3, unofficial]. It was popularized in game development communities (e.g., Stack Overflow, GameDev Stack Exchange) as a standard optimization technique for voxel worlds [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. The approach allows for efficient management of large, dynamic voxel environments by balancing the cost of mesh generation against the cost of draw calls [S2, unofficial].
